    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe spec: *when no registration date is supplied, default it to the server's current date and return `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`*. This is the Spring PetClinic REST app where DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` and mapped to JPA entities via MapStruct, so I threaded the new field through every layer:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, this makes the field both an accepted input on `POST /api/owners` and a returned field on `GET`. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added the `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the DTO to an entity, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null; a supplied date is left untouched. (MapStruct maps the same-named field automatically both directions, so no mapper change was needed.)\n\n4. **Schema files** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to `owners` in all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed data uses positional `INSERT`s, so I appended a `NULL` registration_date to each of the 10 owner rows to match the new column count (h2/postgres use column-named inserts and needed no change). Seed owners keep a null registration date, which is fine since the rule only governs new creates.\n\nBoth tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (no date \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved).",
